<h2>Finding confidence and review</h2>
<p>Assessed at {{ r.assurance.assessed_at }}. Human review is separate from scanner status and change approval.
Reviewer identity: <b>{{ r.assurance.identity_label }}</b>. Suppression is not remediation.</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Raw scanner open</th><th>Confirmed</th><th>Unreviewed</th><th>Suppressed</th><th>Needs investigation</th><th>Risk accepted (remediation held)</th></tr>
<tr><td>{{ r.assurance.counts.raw_open }}</td><td>{{ r.assurance.counts.confirmed }}</td><td>{{ r.assurance.counts.unreviewed }}</td><td>{{ r.assurance.counts.suppressed }}</td><td>{{ r.assurance.counts.needs_investigation }}</td><td>{{ r.assurance.counts.risk_accepted }}</td></tr>
</table>
<p class="meta">Review counts above are subsets of raw-open observations, including discovery. Verified fixes do not rewrite these raw counts.
Scanner pass: {{ r.assurance.counts.scanner_pass }}; scanner not applicable: {{ r.assurance.counts.scanner_not_applicable }};
scanner not reviewed: {{ r.assurance.counts.scanner_not_reviewed }}; scanner errors: {{ r.assurance.counts.scanner_error }}.
Unchecked results and errors are not passes. An unreviewed scanner pass is not a human decision.</p>
<h2>Finding evidence and review</h2>
<p class="meta">All selected scanner observations and current discovery items are retained below, including suppressed findings.
Historical observations use only reviews matching their evidence fingerprint, evaluated at report generation time.</p>
{% for f in r.assurance.findings %}
{% set review = f.review %}
{% set event = review.current or {} %}
<div class="finding-evidence">
<p><b>{{ f.host }}: {{ f.title }}</b> ({{ f.severity }}) | Finding <code>{{ f.id }}</code> | Source: {{ f.source }} | Rule: {{ f.rule_id }}</p>
<p>Original scanner status: <b>{{ f.status }}</b>. {% if review.suppressed %}<b>SUPPRESSED BY REVIEW - NOT REMEDIATED.</b>{% endif %}</p>
<p>Risk acceptance: <b>{{ review.risk_acceptance_status }}</b>. {% if review.remediation_held %}<b>REMEDIATION HELD. Risk remains open; no fix or remediation approval is established.</b>{% endif %}</p>
{% if review.risk_acceptance %}
<p>Recorded risk decision: {{ review.risk_acceptance.disposition }}; actor: {{ review.risk_acceptance.reviewed_by }};
reason: {{ review.risk_acceptance.reason }}; evidence: {{ review.risk_acceptance.supporting_evidence }};
expiry: {{ review.risk_acceptance.expires_at or "none" }};
original evidence fingerprint: <code>{{ review.risk_acceptance.evidence_fingerprint }}</code>.</p>
{% endif %}
<p>Confidence: <b>{{ f.confidence.grade }}</b> - {{ f.confidence.reason }}</p>
<p>Review disposition: <b>{{ review.disposition }}</b>; active: {{ "yes" if review.active else "no" }};
suppressed: {{ "yes" if review.suppressed else "no" }}; reviewer identity: {{ f.identity_label }}.</p>
{% if event %}
<p>Last review disposition: {{ event.disposition }}; reviewer: {{ f.reviewer_identity.text }}; reviewed at: {{ event.reviewed_at }};
expiry: {{ event.expires_at or "none" }}. Reason: {{ event.reason }}</p>
<p>Supporting evidence: {{ event.supporting_evidence or "none supplied" }}</p>
{% else %}
<p>Reviewer: none; reason: no matching review; expiry: none.</p>
{% endif %}
{% if review.reopened_reason %}<p><b>Review reopened:</b> {{ review.reopened_reason }}</p>{% endif %}
<p>Scanner evidence: {{ f.evidence or "not supplied" }}</p>
<p class="meta">Citations: {{ f.citations | join(", ") }}. Evidence fingerprint: <code>{{ review.evidence_fingerprint }}</code>.</p>
</div>
{% else %}
<p>No scanner observations available.</p>
{% endfor %}
